ef 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150827 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "69a5f29a-cfcb-5825-a49b-f6b7a3f7a079" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150828 #edb/ref 1080 "2x_{i} - 9y_{j} + 11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150828 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150828 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "81211187-e429-5762-8da7-4e1bdfa17158" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150829 #edb/ref 1080 "2x_{i} - 9y_{j - 1} + 11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150829 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150829 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d8033161-d57f-51a1-83de-16e5172fc800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150830 #edb/ref 1080 "2x_{i - 1} - 9y_{j - 1} + 11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150830 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150830 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e739ee5c-7ea0-5272-8ba6-4cc713f400aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150831 #edb/ref 1080 "x_{i} - y_{j - 1} + 11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150831 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150831 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f340e40a-0a65-51d5-8dd2-378e02af5d81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150832 #edb/ref 1080 "2x_{i - 1} - 9y_{j} + 11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150832 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186150832 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7c49e799-61a5-5104-bb2d-d888e99d4689" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151941 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6247" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151941 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151941 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "150649f4-8b1e-563a-a774-1857d8781212" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151941 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151942 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151942 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151942 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3923e1d8-73e5-501c-96b5-d6b729260d3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186151942 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) =10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[2,3].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152042 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152042 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [2,3] \\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x - y + 3.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152042 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b3b3c2bc-029c-5128-8ea9-00591c6936d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152042 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})={x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1 \\leq i \\leq m$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186151941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152153 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186151942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152154 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186152720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186259534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186365391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186544875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1039 "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186152042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152232 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186153186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1045 "Lower Riemann Sums Over General Rectangular Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186153052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152327 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "96a53612-ec02-52e7-9961-40c187e6e800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152717 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186150809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152717 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75063" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152717 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [1, 5] \\cdot [2, 7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 100 - x^{2} - y^{2}$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152717 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "579f4499-afd3-5e1e-813e-db4e394ec885" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152718 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186150815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152718 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75092" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152718 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [- 1, 1] \\cdot [- 1, 1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 8 - x - y$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152718 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1cb469e6-7b74-5371-89e3-14f53be7cb3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152720 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186150827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152720 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152720 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R = [0, 1] \\cdot [0, 1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = 2x - 9y + 11$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$L(f, P) = ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)AAAAAΔx_{i}Δy_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186152720 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3919f4a6-1144-5c7c-8ecf-d772c823e93b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153048 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153048 #edb/ref 1061 23452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153048 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "30e60cbf-4794-5b51-be6a-93b451386c0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153048 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153049 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153049 #edb/ref 1061 23454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153049 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5f845909-7a57-5bcc-b7ec-58d8bd3178cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153049 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153052 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186153048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153052 #edb/ref 1061 23479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153052 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e1b4e0b9-1f1d-5d68-a2bc-6a50156f08de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153052 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186153351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153186 #edb/ref 1061 35555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153186 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "85ace4fd-3ba9-514e-a57a-7f919b2ae2a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153186 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153351 #edb/ref 1064 "We know how to write the lower Riemann sum for a function $f(x,y)$ over a *fixed* rectangular partition. In this lesson, we will learn how to write down an expression for the lower Riemann sum for an *arbitrary* rectangular partition. \n\nAs a concrete example, let $R = [0,1] \\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and define the function $f(x,y)$ as \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = x^2+y^2.\n$$\n\nFurther, let $P$ be an arbitrary partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur goal is to find an expression for $L(f, P),$ the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition. We proceed identically to the case where $P$ was fixed.\n\nFirst, we consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{j-1}$ and $y_j$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nSince we're computing the *lower* sum, we're interested in the *minimum* value of $f$ in this subregion.\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x^2+y^2$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,1],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x^2+y^2$ increases as $y$ increases on $[0,1].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nTherefore, the *minimum* value of $f$ in the subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value of $f$ at the *bottom left corner* of the subregion.\n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nSo, if $m_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion, we have\n\n$$\nm_{ij} = f(x_{i-1}, y_{j-1}) = x_{i-1}^2 + y_{j-1}^2\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$ \n\nSince the area of $R_{ij}$ is $\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j,$ the volume of the rectangular solid with base $R_{ij}$ and height $m_{ij}$ is\n\n$$\nm_{ij}\\Delta x_i\\Delta y_j = (x_{i-1}^2 + y_{j-1}^2)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j \\, .\n$$\n\nFinally, summing up all of our rectangular solids over the entire partition $P$, we find that the lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P) = \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_{i-1}^2 + y_{j-1}^2)\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j \\, .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153351 #edb/ref 1065 3958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153351 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0ef8305a-8a99-57ba-8aee-063624e8571a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186153351 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257197 #edb/ref 1080 "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j-1}+20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257197 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257197 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2ede9bce-ae38-577e-bacc-87f020612226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257668 #edb/ref 1080 "5{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}+20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257668 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186257668 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6500c138-a000-5c85-b486-9284962f6b24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258243 #edb/ref 1080 "-{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258243 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258243 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a76fe671-7d45-5709-aab4-68d346881651" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258312 #edb/ref 1080 "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258312 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258312 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "afb8a0b8-c91b-53d8-92d2-f3dd9be2ef32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258871 #edb/ref 1080 "{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258871 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186258871 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f02ab099-1461-5c8c-8a64-5841486261ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186257668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186258871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186258312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259451 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f121ff54-6918-5739-ba1a-2bd0e425da2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259532 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186259451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259532 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123513" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259532 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259532 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259532 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e6e7588-d998-5d13-bde2-9f1ecbe236a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259532 #edb/ref 1074 "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544090 #edb/ref 1080 "3{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544090 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544090 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02467f85-cb8c-52e6-8524-d58170a0e13a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544091 #edb/ref 1080 "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544091 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544091 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544131 #edb/ref 1080 "9{y}_{j-1}+2{x}_{i}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544131 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544131 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "138fc8d0-58bb-56a7-a4a1-0ead87eb84d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544190 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}+10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544190 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544190 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f75718e-b688-57f7-8da7-5b80fb085343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544238 #edb/ref 1080 "5{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544238 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544238 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45327c1c-8d20-5959-acce-f569c289c1cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544244 #edb/ref 1080 "16-{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544244 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544244 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "475cfc3a-6171-510d-b62d-087df74508ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544255 #edb/ref 1080 "11{y}_{j-1}-6{x}_{i}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544255 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544255 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d